Metadata-Version: 2.1
Name: torchao
Version: 0.0.0

Stub metadata for the verl torchao stub package (see
verl/workers/engine/automodel/utils.py::_ensure_torchao_stub).

transformers' `_is_package_available("torchao")` uses importlib.util.find_spec
to detect the package (our stub dir is on sys.path, so the spec is found) and
importlib.metadata.version to read its version. Without a dist-info,
version() raises PackageNotFoundError and transformers keeps version "N/A"
with availability True, which later crashes packaging.version.parse in
is_torchao_available() (killed SGLang scheduler spawn children during
unpickle-time transformers import).

With this dist-info, importlib.metadata.version("torchao") returns "0.0.0" --
a valid version below transformers' minimum torchao requirement, so
is_torchao_available() cleanly returns False and the stub keeps
HAVE_TORCHAO-style probes False.
